  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="17">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Iudex">Iudex</ref> 17</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="17" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="476" ed="#liebermann"/>Susceptio muneris dimissio est ueritatis.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="476" ed="#liebermann"/>Seo anfengnes medsceata on domum ys soðfæstnesse forlætnes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="476" ed="#liebermann"/>Die Annahme von Lohngeldern bei Rechtssprüchen ist das Verlassen der Wahrhaftigkeit.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">The acceptance of bribes in judgments is the abandoning of truthfulness.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-g-a">The acceptance of bribes for judgements is the abandonment of truth.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="476">Isidor, Sent. III 54.3; <ref target="clause:Iudex_4">Iudex 4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 54, 3 | (vgl. o. 4)</note>
        <note type="editorial">Isidore, Sent. III 54.3; compare 4. In the Quadripartitus, II Eg follows.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
